description: |
  Confirm system call fuzz testing is being performed.
  The database is checked at the end to ensure each entry was executed at least once.
  Default runtime is 1 hour (3600 seconds), but can be changed using the "time" environment variable.
  Test inputs:
      A list with the sysfs entries to be fuzzed, and a fuzzer program
      called syzkaller. Input details:
      - sycalls list (environment variable `enable_syscalls`)
      - syzkaller code: https://github.com/google/syzkaller
      - check for execution: grep -q "^${syscall}[$,(]" "${local_dir}"/corpus_dir/*
  Expected results:
      If the system calls are executed without incident during the test runtime,
      all syscalls in list should be executed at least once. Example:
      [   PASS   ] :: No crash results found.
      [   PASS   ] :: [syscall_name] executed.
contact: Pablo Ridolfi <pridolfi@redhat.com>
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - gcc
  - gcc-c++
  - git
  - glibc
  - glibc-common
  - glibc-devel
  - make
  - patch
  - sshpass
  - tar
  - tmux
  - wget
  - type: file
    pattern:
        - /kernel-include
        - /syzkaller
        - /misc/fuzz_sysfs_procfs
duration: 3h
environment:
  time: 3600
  RHIVOS_LATENCY_THRES: 50000
